    <h1>Teaching Resources</h1>
    <p>Resources for librarians, educators, and faculty to assist with teaching using JSTOR.</p>
    
    <h2>Lesson Plans and Handouts</h2>
    <p>Our lesson plans and handouts can be copied and adapted for your own use as needed. Each lesson plan contains key points about JSTOR's features, suggested activities for students, and links to relevant training videos and support pages. We will periodically update these resources as the JSTOR platform continues to evolve.</p>
    <ul>
      <li title="View Research on JSTOR in Google Docs"><a href="https://docs.google.com/document/d/11S5KRYeUVOq56ZZY5Q1dQv-euKiKW4LV4KUmB-04gQQ/edit?usp=sharing">Research on JSTOR</a> (Google Docs)</li>
            <li title="Make a copy of Images on JSTOR in Google Slides"><a href="https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1IMExyQW1jTz7iZOfSh647E3uxZOM8I-R1IcjRDdHjZY/copy">Images on JSTOR</a> (Google Slides)</li>
      <li title="Download JSTOR Quick Start Guide PDF"><a href="https://support.jstor.org/hc/article_attachments/30144157041431">JSTOR Quick Start Guide</a> (PDF)</li>
    </ul>
    
    <h2>LibGuides</h2>
    <p>All of our guides are open and free, and Springshare library customers are welcome to copy our guides to their own LibGuides sites and customize them with library branding and additional information.</p>
    <ul>
      <li title="How to Use JSTOR LibGuide"><a href="https://guides.jstor.org/how-to-jstor/welcome">How to Use JSTOR</a></li>
      <li title="Images on JSTOR LibGuide"><a href="https://guides.jstor.org/images">Images on JSTOR (including Artstor)</a></li>
      <li title="JSTOR for Secondary Schools LibGuide"><a href="https://guides.jstor.org/secondary-schools">JSTOR for Secondary Schools</a></li>
      <li title="JSTOR Subjects and Collections Guide LibGuide"><a href="https://guides.jstor.org/subjects-collections">JSTOR Subjects and Collections Guide</a></li>
    </ul>
    
